# The caller binds a method's free name by its own binding at the call; with
# none, the name falls back to the declaration the method sees. mid stands
# under the store of h2 and calls it. over stands above the store and holds a
# callable of its own under the name: mid, called from over, calls that one,
# 300 + 12. plain stands above the store and has no h2: mid, called from
# plain, calls the unit's, 100 + 12, as it does called from the root.
# Entry 7.
fn: make2 (int: n) fn: (int: x; int: y) int
    fn: f2 (int: x; int: y) int
        return: n + x * 10 + y
    return: f2

fn: over () int
    h2: make2 300
    return: mid()
end: over

fn: plain () int
    return: mid()
end: plain

h2: make2 100

fn: mid () int
    return: h2(1 2)
end: mid

int: a over()
int: b plain()
int: c mid()
int: ok 7
if: a != 312
    ok: 81
if: b != 112
    ok: 82
if: c != 112
    ok: 83
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
